{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>For there was no house.</b> We say in the Sifrei: would it enter your mind that there was no house in which there was no firstborn? Rather, such was the custom of the Egyptians: when their firstborn died, they would make an icon of him in their houses, and at that moment it would shatter and fall to the ground, and it was as hard in their eyes as the day of death. And further we say there: in the place where their firstborns were buried, mice would come and dig after them and drag them out, and it was harder for them than the day of death."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:04.314455222Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}